WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.879
Most popular television characters get the
close-up treatment throughout the course of

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.420
a TV series… but there are a few fan favorites
whose faces we never get to see.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.000
"Where you going?"

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.080
"Nooooo…"

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.220
Let's take a look - or at least have a listen
- at some faceless TV characters who still

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.380
managed to make a lasting impression.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.820
Wilson on Home Improvement

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.260
"Wilson, what are you doing?"

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.840
"I'm just testing my maracas."

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.100
"Usually when I have mine tested, the doctor
makes me turn my head and cough."

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.390
Tim Taylor's trusty next-door neighbor on
Home Improvement was always futzing around

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.280
in his backyard.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:42.520
Improbably named Wilson W. Wilson, the good-natured
goof inspired some of the show's most groan-inducing

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.020
jokes.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.280
"What are you doing, Wilson?"

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.280
"Well, Tim, I'm admiring my yams."

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.380
"Should I leave you alone?"

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.910
During the course of the show, Wilson's face
was always partially concealed, usually behind

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:55.480
a fence.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.680
"Wilson, what are you doing up?"

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.020
"Well, Tim, I couldn't sleep so I thought
I'd come out and squeeze my apples."

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.340
The character was reportedly inspired by Tim
Allen's real-life neighbor growing up… when

00:01:08.341 --> 00:01:11.729
he was still too short to see over the fence
and catch a glimpse at his full face.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:16.670
After hiding from audiences for eight seasons,
actor Earl Hindman finally revealed his face

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.900
in the at the final curtain call.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.900
"Playing Wilson is Earl Hindman!"

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.180
Maris Crane on Frasier

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.720
"I'm supposed to ask Maris to spend an evening
with a baseball player?

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.720
Why don't I just ask her to 'rub my shoulders?'"

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:36.780
Niles Crane's former wife Maris wasn't supposed
to be concealed from Frasier viewers forever,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.460
but the character's description quickly became
too bizarre to cast: generally pale, skeletal,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.270
tiny, and altogether too strange to be human…
before later becoming morbidly obese.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.840
Executive producers Peter Casey and David
Lee explained in a Season 2 DVD extra:

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.520
"Well, some of the things that had been written
about her in scripts, I don't know if we could

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.100
ever find anybody that would match all those
things."

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.340
In the Season 5 episode "Voyage of the Damned,"
audiences did get to see a shadow of Maris

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.460
behind a shower curtain:

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.140
[gargling]

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.370
We wonder if David Hyde Pierce is still waiting
for that zany Maris spinoff.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.860
"When we go off the air, whenever it is, she'll
probably have her own show."

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.860
Mrs. Wolowitz on The Big Bang Theory

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.540
"Howard, the phone is ringing!"

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.360
"Here's a crazy idea, ma, answer it!"

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.280
Howard Wolowitz's elusive mother on The Big
Bang Theory was voiced by the late actress

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.560
Carol Ann Susi... which you can totally hear
in her Season 5 appearance in Grey's Anatomy:

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.560
"No, she's the mean one!

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:43.700
I don't want her!"

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.870
Debbie Wolowitz is described as a large woman
with a mustache and curly black hair... but

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.769
that wasn't in keeping with the appearance
of the actress who voiced her.

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:56.680
In Big Bang Theory's Season 5 finale, we do
briefly see Mrs. Wolowitz in an overhead shot.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.209
We also catch a very brief glimpse of her
in the Season 15 episode "The Spoiler Alert

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:02.200
Segmentation."

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:03.100
"What's wrong?"

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.640
"My mom died."

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:12.400
When Carol Ann Susi sadly passed in 2014,
writers decided Howard's mother would die,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:12.900
too.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.480
Still, her memory lives on.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.780
"Nobody likes the pancakes?"

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.840
"He didn't try them yet!"

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.940
Ugly Naked Guy on Friends

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:24.840
"Huh."

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:25.500
"What?"

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.720
"Ugly Naked Guy looks awfully still."

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.960
We never learn the real name of Ugly Naked
Guy on Friends, but we certainly get to know

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.460
him:

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.640
"I'm sorry, I can't help but notice that you're
naked."

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.800
In a Season Three episode, the gang even pokes
their bizarre nudist neighbor with a rubber-banded

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.340
batch of chopsticks... because they think
he's dead.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.500
"He's alive, he's alive!"

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.560
In another Season Three episode, we learn
via flashback that Ugly Naked Guy had a very

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.120
different nickname three years earlier:

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.160
"Oh that is so unfortunate."

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:06.200
"What?"

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.380
"Cute Naked Guy is really starting to put
on weight."

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.760
The actor who played Ugly Naked Guy remained
a pop-culture mystery for decades… until

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.489
HuffPo writer Todd Van Luling cracked the
case in 2016.

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:20.980
Meet the man, the myth, the legend… actor
Jon Haugen.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.080
He says it took him awhile to come forward
because he was "keeping it mellow."

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.630
Plus, Warner Bros. reportedly wanted everybody
to guess who had played the role.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.860
That's so Ugly Naked Guy.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.520
George Steinbrenner on Seinfeld

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.240
"All right, let's see what I have today.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.500
Oh, darn it, it's ham and cheese again.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.420
And she forgot the fancy mustard!"

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:43.640
It's rare for a scripted sitcom to feature
an impression of a real public figure, so

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.710
when George Costanza wound up working for
Yankees guru George Steinbrenner on Seinfeld,

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:49.830
the approach was simple.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.870
They only showed Steinbrenner from behind,
with actor Lee Bear appearing as the back

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.500
of his head, and creator Larry David voicing
the role.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:01.020
The real Steinbrenner loved the schtick so
much, he agreed to tape a cameo as himself.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.280
That cameo never aired, but his scenes eventually
made their way onto a Seinfeld DVD.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.340
"Wait a minute, young lady, what's this about
singles' tables?

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.700
I don't sit at singles tables!

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.260
Singles tables are for losers!"

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.880
Now let's compare and contrast.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.860
"Want me to say it again, I'll say it again!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.880
I haven't had a pimple since I was 18, and
I don't care if you believe me or not.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:19.140
And how's this, you're fired!"

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.500
Isn't it uncanny?

